Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Chern-Simons Theory", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This paclet contains computable aspects of a version of ",
 StyleBox["Chern-Simons theory",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " announced by ",
 ButtonBox["Cieliebak, Fukaya and Latschev",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1508.02741"], None}],
 ", defined by ",
 ButtonBox["Cieliebak and Volkov",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.05922"], None}],
 " and, among others, studied in ",
 ButtonBox["H\[AAcute]jek's PhD thesis",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.07933"], None}],
 ". It corresponds to the ",
 StyleBox["large-",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"72733162-6c8b-4494-8506-f30767154e38"],
 StyleBox[" limit",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], "(", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"cf492e13-f752-4b28-ad39-dd63d93763a8"],
 " Chern-Simons theory on a closed oriented manifold (see also the recent \
paper of ",
 ButtonBox["Hamilton",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.15938"], None}],
 ")."
}], "GuideAbstract",ExpressionUUID->"3b0202d3-ce5d-4d18-becb-b253c8cc5683"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It can be formulated on the ",
 StyleBox["cyclic words",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " of the de Rham cohomology either as an IBL-infinity ",
 StyleBox["Maurer-Cartan element",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " of a ",
 StyleBox["canonical involutive bi-Lie algebra",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (IBL), or equivalently, as a ",
 StyleBox["Beilinson-Drinfeld action",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " of a ",
 StyleBox["canonical BD operator",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". The action defines an ",
 StyleBox["open string field theory",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " on the de Rham cohomology that corresponds to a ",
 StyleBox["quantum A-infinity algebra",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " generalizing ",
 ButtonBox["Stasheff",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-1963-0158400-5"], None}],
 "'s ",
 StyleBox["A-infinity homotopy transfer",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " from trees to ",
 StyleBox["trivalent ribbon graphs",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (see ",
 ButtonBox["M\[UDoubleDot]nster and Sachs",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1109.4101"], None}],
 ")."
}], "GuideAbstract",ExpressionUUID->"2f43d31e-0fb7-41c8-bd3d-e6a1058b4d9b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This open string field theory can be thought of as the open sector of an ",
 StyleBox["open-closed string field theory",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (",
 ButtonBox["M\[UDoubleDot]nster and Sachs",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1303.3444"], None}],
 "), with the closed part being the ",
 StyleBox["symplectic field theory",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " of the unit cotangent bundle, and the ",
 StyleBox["IBL-infinity morphism",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " between the canonical IBL algebra twisted by the Maurer-Cartan element and \
the IBL-infinity algebra of symplectic field theory twisted by the canonical \
augmentation being obtained by integrating forms over the ",
 StyleBox["moduli spaces of holomorphic curves",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " with boundary punctures on the zero section (open string insertions), \
where the forms are pulled back, and interior punctures asymptotic to Reeb \
orbits (closed string insertions)."
}], "GuideAbstract",ExpressionUUID->"46c0dd44-a743-4309-b792-accce04ddd58"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "If the manifold is simply connected, the structure is related to ",
 StyleBox["string topology",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": the twisted IBL-infinity algebra is a chain model of ",
 StyleBox["Chas-Sullivan equivariant string topology",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " relative to a base point, via ",
 StyleBox["Chen's iterated integrals",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". If the manifold is homologically simply connected, strong vanishing \
results hold (",
 ButtonBox["Cieliebak, H\[AAcute]jek and Volkov",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.06837"], None}],
 ") and the structure can be equivalently computed by taking a ",
 StyleBox["Poincar\[EAcute] duality model",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " of the de Rham cohomology and the canonical IBL algebra on its cyclic \
words equipped with the ",
 StyleBox["cyclic Hochschild differential",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "."
}], "GuideAbstract",ExpressionUUID->"d09d2ba2-f636-4208-bf8b-da3b58e9abfb"]
}, Open  ]],

